# Lunowix — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. Everything here is optional in
# development; the two marked REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION are not.
#
# Check a deployment with `curl https://your-site/api/health` — it reports
# which store is live and whether sessions can be signed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sessions — REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs the session cookie. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Must be at least 32 characters. Without it, `next start` refuses to sign
# sessions and every sign-in and registration fails — deliberately, because the
# alternatives are worse: a random per-process key would sign cookies the next
# deploy could not verify, quietly signing everyone out at intervals, and a
# hardcoded default would mint valid sessions for anyone who knew it.
#
# Changing it signs everybody out. That is also how you revoke every session.
AUTH_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any Postgres connection string. The free tiers all work: Neon, Supabase,
# Railway, Render.
#
# Unset, the app uses a JSON file store under `.data/` — which is right for
# development and wrong for a serverless host, where each request gets a fresh
# filesystem and writes do not survive. On Vercel, Netlify or Lambda the app
# refuses to start on the file store rather than losing data silently.
DATABASE_URL=

# TLS to the database. `relaxed` (the default) encrypts without verifying the
# server certificate, which is what every managed provider's own snippet does.
# `verify` requires a valid chain — set PGSSLROOTCERT too. `disable` for a local
# plaintext container.
#
# Any `sslmode` in DATABASE_URL is STRIPPED and this decides instead. Providers
# all append `?sslmode=require`, which the driver treats as `verify-full` and
# which used to silently override this setting — so a provider whose certificate
# the app has no root for failed with a bare "self-signed certificate".
# DATABASE_SSL=relaxed

# Connections per process. Free tiers cap this hard, and serverless multiplies
# the process count.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=5

# Overrides where the JSON file store writes. Development convenience.
# LUNOWIX_DATA_DIR=.data

# Allows the file store on a platform detected as serverless. Only set this if
# the instance really has a persistent disk.
# LUNOWIX_ALLOW_FILE_STORE=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute origin, used by the sitemap, robots.txt, canonical tags, the OG card
# and the password-reset link. Falls back to http://localhost:3000, which is
# wrong in production and quietly bad for SEO.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mail (Resend) — optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without these the contact form returns 501 and says nothing was sent, and
# password reset returns 501 rather than claiming an email is on its way.
# Until you verify a domain, Resend only delivers to the address you signed up
# with.
RESEND_API_KEY=
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=Lunowix <hello@yourdomain.com>
